Package: searchengine-gpu-control
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Your Name <your-email@example.com>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), systemd
Description: GPU control service for SE's Vision (image/video generation) mode
 A small, root-privileged HTTP control service, installed only on the
 dedicated GPU host, that switches the shared GPU between its normal
 chat role (vllm-chat.service) and image/video generation
 (comfyui.service, LTX-2.5), since both can't fit in VRAM at once. See
 https://github.com/M0WA/SE/blob/main/packaging/gpu-control/README.md.
 .
 Deliberately packaged separately from the main searchengine package --
 it runs as root and holds a distinct secret (GPU_CONTROL_TOKEN), neither
 of which the main search/admin/crawl host should have.
